\f1\fs22 The first thing Tony explained to Hayley was the source of the adornments of flowers, the table of remaining muffin baskets, and the boxes of sex toys stacked like an impromptu warehouse in back of the couch in the parlour. Alexander sat, relaxed and rather pleased with himself, in a comfy single-seater with two Elvi standing over from behind. It seemed he genuinely believed his obsessive and somewhat inappropriate gifting put him in the light of an earnest romantic suitor rather than a deranged stalker.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy tended to Sarah in her upstairs room while Tony put the pieces together for Hayley in the typical oversharing manner of a genuine innocent eager to lift the eye of the law from gazing in his direction. At one point, Hayley asked Tony, \'91Did you take any documents from the office where Travis Teh died?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No, I never took any documents,\'92 Tony said, and Hayley sensed the gritty mote of a lie in what sounded essentially truthful.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Did you take anything, anything at all?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The only things I took were exploded body parts, and my own cleaning equipment and supplies.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>That sounded truer, but Hayley still didn\'92t like it. \'91Then why does Agent Jones believe you did?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I honestly have no idea, detective.\'92 For Tony\'92s part, he knew Agent Jones was looking for that accursed disc which he guessed Sarah still possessed. He could honestly state he didn\'92t steal documents or anything else from the suicide scene.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91He\'92s very convinced you did. He broke into your apartment and attacked you. Somehow, you and Sarah escaped.\'92 Alexander moaned in emotional pain; Hayley continued. \'91He pursued you to the 
\f2\i Memphis Mafia Bar
\f1\i0 , where you again escaped, this time with the resolute help of the Elvi. And here you both are now, ensconced in this mansion, defended by tanks, apparently some kind of revered royalty, the Holy Momma and the Great Teacher.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91All I know, detective, is they like the lyrics I write, and their songs are now very popular.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91They are indeed,\'92 Hayley conceded. \'91Mr Supaporn, are you the father of Sarah Jacobson\'92s baby?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No!\'92 Tony and Alexander protested. As Alexander sat on the edge of his seat, Tony bitterly added, \'91She\'92s much too good for me.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After a full interview, Hayley thanked Tony and dismissed him. She\'92d call for Sarah soon, but there was still Alexander to manage.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Satisfied?\'92 Hayley asked him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander crossed his legs and stroked his index finger down his top lip all the way to the corner of his mouth. He poised the finger, as if about to make a point, stopped himself\'97mouth half-open, finger wilting into a curl\'97while he rewrote the script in his head. After a moment, his eyebrows became decisive and the finger re-erected. \'91I owe you an apology, detective\'85 inspector.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>While Hayley savoured the victory, she remained wary.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I\'92d be happy to have contracts drawn up today, to secure the rights to these story arcs you\'92ve devised.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Story arcs? It\'92s the simple truth.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You are so passionately dedicated to your craft, detective inspector, and I want you to know I respect that. I once thought the entertainment industry would crush your idealism, but I see now you possess a genuine talent. And\'97and let me warn you, I think I\'92m about to say something, with your permission, and I am completely sincere\'97completely sincere\'97in a way that\'92s usually reserved for praise of my own unparalleled work\'85 oh, look\'85 shall I just come out and say it?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Please do.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You are a genius, Detective Inspector Hayley Lanning. A genius!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91A genius\'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Own it, Hayley-kins. There\'92s no need to be self-deprecating. My ego can take the hit.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well, whenever your ego needs a hit, let me know.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Again with the self-deprecating humour, Hayley-puss. I never realised it could be so charming. I wonder if I can work it into my own schtick\'85\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Why mess with your brand?\'92 Hayley said. \'91It works.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander\'92s eyes lit up and he chuckled. \'91Ha! You\'92re right, of course. But look, I really must\'97humbly, to the extent my breeding allows\'97thank you for what you\'92ve done here.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And what\'92s that?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92ve lifted the story up, Holly-girl! That\'92s what you\'92ve done. Here I was machinating over a tawdry local-terrorist-come-kidnapper story, and you\'92ve transcended all that! Transcended! The scale now seeps into the darkest halls of power in this country, into the deep state of the nation, and shines sunlight on the corruption and back-room clock-tampering of the most secretive agency in the country.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The Global Stasis Technicians Association?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander laughed. \'91Fridge Force? Very funny, but no\'85 well, maybe\'85 no\'85 we\'92ll work them in for season two. Let\'92s focus on what\'92s got me all jolly about this collaboration, Helly-Whiskers. It\'92s a story about how our very own police department exposes a plot by PAPER to control the halls of power by scaring the populace with vexatious terrorism threats and framing innocent nobodies for crimes they never committed. And we\'92ll uncover it all!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well, that\'92s kinda where I was going with this all along.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I see that now! You are a true narrative genius, Detective Inspector Executive Producer Holy Lamingtons.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Oh, sister, was all Hayley thought.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander was too busy constructing his own grandiose visions to notice Hayley disengaging. But then he sobered as a new thought struck him. \'91You know what?\'92 he said, cutting off any chance for her to answer. \'91I\'92m really glad you got Tony off the hook. He\'92s really a very good friend.\'92
